[{"id":"VRCE-3-8-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":1,"english":"When the son of Raghu had set out with Sutiksna's permission, SItā addressed him in affectionate words and convincing speech.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4df606f21373bab127fd412d6244e03081279a306a0c25cbcda8a69ddf74e5f9","compact":"6604f456b62ea4e01a245a67ba5721bf8687921e8107db46db07b6ab9e4b96aa","nasal":"4e1db111be9a81b1b95e50d67ed791ca3eb14569fa128da1fdb46173adda49fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":2,"english":"Although you are great and follow the narrow way (of righteousness), yet you are on the eve of entering into unrighteousness. But you could by refraining from action, eschew this unrighteousness that springs from an evil begot of desire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cc57b7c09cbee00fca91c387936eb5b06dd4fa7dd0f82149a7b55487d8729618","compact":"5f64bbe00a2dc806cfb83188e80624dee5286dc3de80f91fdd2ecc1f90a37688","nasal":"3404342ff9217c5c338f26a691db3cf6e95af0635ed6b633e5bdb4ee4a6c06ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":3,"english":"This evil begot of desire is threefold. One prominent evil is falsehood, and both the others' are of weightier significance, association with others; wives, and vindictiveness without any (basis of) hostility. Falsehood, O Rāghava, has never been yours nor can it ever be yours (in the future).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da758a8dc0e9c03a27ece1eeeea9f45b6a80fcf6ea65cdf044fcd5f2ab5307f9","compact":"70ddbd3ccb9d9ad385c3ebabb3a76827e76f619d0912dcc53a0ae344ef2ee5d5","nasal":"42aa527963a6a2fcdffd2aff4dbc72f59ab88252610b472022259c954bbc0d2b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":4,"english":"This evil begot of desire is threefold. One prominent evil is falsehood, and both the others' are of weightier significance, association with others; wives, and vindictiveness without any (basis of) hostility. Falsehood, O Rāghava, has never been yours nor can it ever be yours (in the future). Nor yet, O foremost of men, can you ever even in fancy be (guilty of) going after others' wives, which destroy all religious merit. These, O Rāma, are by no means in you. O King's son, you ever and a day direct your attentions to own wife. And you are Righteous and truthful and do the will of your şire. In you are established virtue and truth, and every thing; and by help of your conquered senses, you, O mighty armed one, are capable of bearing everything.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-3","DUTT-3-9-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54579e480f7776b2dbbc23e8b06ebf8941e0e596693433a18679805d984a481e","compact":"2dfd5ac561447398e11f1b38e3812c3339e604fd9464b1a23bb6b5c2caf512c5","nasal":"2dfd5ac561447398e11f1b38e3812c3339e604fd9464b1a23bb6b5c2caf512c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":5,"english":"O you of a gracious presence, yours is control over sense. The third evil that leads men through ignorance to bear hostility towards others without any (cause of) hostility, is now present (to you).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b000fdfd78d21ebbb0e81aad91f1999e49330d0c17d89e62a9c435164226ee11","compact":"f199c1fce215397b2e2ba83939e27eb0451955ef5445878e38e9b1807d99dc38","nasal":"9d71007aa38b7b9d7017cf1d8ba7c01174b33f7c32fbe376235df669876fc4b6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":6,"english":"O you of a gracious presence, yours is control over sense. The third evil that leads men through ignorance to bear hostility towards others without any (cause of) hostility, is now present (to you).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1620d1cb83928008fa8257b1dfdd960073b8778cb2d8b93122f4ce3849ab35dc","compact":"20ae95f3cc2f45c221f2232958b11d97e16ae4dc6b7ad6801bcc279786285e2e","nasal":"20ae95f3cc2f45c221f2232958b11d97e16ae4dc6b7ad6801bcc279786285e2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":7,"english":"You have, O hero, for the protection of the saints dwelling in the forest of Dandaka, Promised the slaughter of Rākṣasas in battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"665d2a3a445ccbcb63c4872af918e34e88bbda167f6e046115704e3309f18276","compact":"82715f468eb638664ec5774be34e01ebbe1719a969811948fe2646039cd1c9df","nasal":"31abc22503e105e79c37a3eed68cafaf465866be7100e53e96d0b4d482d83094"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":8,"english":"And it is for this reason that equipped with bows and arrows, you have along with your brother set out for the forest known as Dandaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3637d6f7f60e6801de930efe522f567382e083bc816b58064dfed2d2bea18755","compact":"db12049cc471f11b39d3f27db6f320223766794e161ed60d2d2a4d36b06d726e","nasal":"dd5849d8ee09ce3564099ff8b54fcc958ecf4b790f563093acf37c3214190598"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":9,"english":"Seeing you set out, my mind reflecting on your truthfulness as well as your happiness in this world and welfare in the next, is wrought up with anxiety.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41ec0e502c37428d8930b22aaf1159d1d5c0788590f9d7bfd80f9d5e3ca00856","compact":"e577b141bec95fb5654f559b7fe5b4c5dac82437f931951e86c90d5ff4edd55a","nasal":"bfb390d4c838a87344df967b4d0bd67cb21bd8e5a179f075ca3c0741576a7f3e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":10,"english":"O hero, I do not relish this journey to Dandaka. Thereof I will tell you the reason. Do you listen to me as I tell you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3dfcbf1dcadd0d355e580e7a2fd0580ee5ed0335978f18732ef3593e6ab27f26","compact":"b1ebab565cb5c47050d0e03e1a65fc3a51eea2fa7982c74e4716b3cc4b05d0fe","nasal":"a3820f137ded45ff1bdfbb94e287321d2ab9d1c7ce9a5522d86c1b150fa99f0b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":11,"english":"Bearing bows and arrows in your hands, you have come to the wood along with your brother; and it may well happen) that seeing grim rangers of the forest, you may discharge your shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.74,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5929b4a0dc03c3d09d6d8ba985954aec1834ea0f038e36661f83896f160335a2","compact":"406e3a974ed4d29054fbd4ae849c4d155d5e9a9a9819921878f440ad0ca27540","nasal":"406e3a974ed4d29054fbd4ae849c4d155d5e9a9a9819921878f440ad0ca27540"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":12,"english":"Even as the vicinity of faggots increases the energy of fire, the proximity of (the bow) enhances the strength and energy of the Ksatriya.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd4c4f4844d50ce7d63ffa6dd9f9224ac44cf045695d8ebadba3f8c5176905db","compact":"f6de45676fe9395ba2a39f6a74a1ada8371700dbb510e4248c6e60a7e4ecd63f","nasal":"bc14a9b53c206aab8e269814711ddfb318917619744e7889dab6bdc00f68d3e1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-8-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":8,"verse":13,"english":"Formerly, O long-armed one, in a sacred wood haunted by beasts and birds, there lived a truthful ascetic of a pure person.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-9-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3008013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab396b832fa856153f6edef45e23d817da14670fd71ca